<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "The tab bar at the bottom of the chat area holds the things that can occupy the conversation region: Status, the one conversation you are reading, and — when that conversation has one — its Space. It is a switch between those, not a list of everything you have open."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_star}>{dgettext("help_ui", "Switching Conversations")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Use the conversations sidebar on the left to move between channels and private messages. Click a conversation there and it takes the screen, replacing whichever one the tab bar was showing."
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "From the keyboard, Ctrl+Shift+] and Ctrl+Shift+[ walk through your joined channels and open private messages without touching the mouse."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_channel}>
  {dgettext("help_ui", "Switching Away vs Leaving")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Reading something else does not leave the channel. A conversation you switch away from keeps receiving messages, keeps counting unread, and keeps flashing and playing its sound in the sidebar — you simply are not looking at it."
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "To actually leave, use the × on the tab, or right-click the channel in the sidebar and choose Leave Channel."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_toolbar_community}>{dgettext("help_ui", "Space")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Space is a second view of the conversation you are already in, not a place of its own: the map replaces the messages and the message box keeps working. Switching to another conversation always lands you on its chat, so you never arrive in a map you did not ask for."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_settings}>{dgettext("help_ui", "Buttons Beside the Tabs")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "The controls next to the tabs open something beside the conversation rather than replacing it: channel settings, user lookup, the conference and the P2P session. Each carries its label, so you can read what it does. On a phone the first two also slide the conversations and user list open over the chat."
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Find is not one of them — it lives in Edit > Find, in the Start menu, and on Ctrl+Shift+F."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_ui", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="ui-conversations">{dgettext("help_ui", "Conversations")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="ui-status-tab">{dgettext("help_ui", "Status Tab")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="keyboard-shortcuts">{dgettext("help_ui", "Keyboard Shortcuts")}</.help_link>
</p>
